  val EVENT_1: String = """{"id":"3,280","Title":"How a group of teachers improved their teaching skills through test classrooms and worksheets","User name":"Kunal","designation":"Teacher","location":"Patna, Bihar","District":"Patna","organization":"DPS School","Report Created At":"July 3, 2025, 7:03 AM","objective":"To enhance teacher skills and improve student performance","Challenges":"Teachers were not teaching well due to weak subject knowledge and difficulty in clearing doubts","Action Steps":"['Created test worksheets for teachers to improve their skills', 'Provided a test classroom for teachers to practice and improve their doubt-clearing abilities', 'Assigned worksheets based on teacher experience to ensure effectiveness']","impact":"Teachers showed significant improvement in their teaching skills, leading to better student performance","duration":"1 month","blurb":"I addressed the issue of teachers not teaching well at my school by providing them with test worksheets and a test classroom to improve their skills. After a month, I noticed significant improvement in their teaching. I enjoyed the process despite the challenges.","masked_blurb":"I addressed the issue of teachers not teaching well at my school by providing them with test worksheets and a test classroom to improve their skills. After a month, I noticed significant improvement in their teaching. I enjoyed the process despite the challenges.","content":"Kunal, a teacher at DPS School in Patna, Bihar, noticed that the teachers were not teaching well, resulting in low marks for the students. He identified the reason for this problem as the teachers' weak scale and difficulty in clearing doubts. To solve this, Kunal gave the teachers test worksheets to improve their scale and also provided a test classroom for them to practice. He faced challenges such as the teachers finding the worksheets difficult and lacking interest, but overcame them by giving different worksheets based on their experience. With the help of other teachers and children, Kunal prepared the test classroom and worksheets. It took him about a month to complete this solution. After implementing these steps, Kunal noticed significant improvement in the teachers' skills and their ability to teach well. He enjoyed the process despite the challenges and found the end result to be quite good.","masked_content":"A teacher at DPS School in Patna, Bihar, noticed that the teachers were not teaching well, resulting in low marks for the students. The teacher identified the reason for this problem as the teachers' weak scale and difficulty in clearing doubts. To solve this, the teacher gave the teachers test worksheets to improve their scale and also provided a test classroom for them to practice. The teacher faced challenges such as the teachers finding the worksheets difficult and lacking interest, but overcame them by giving different worksheets based on their experience. With the help of other teachers and children, the teacher prepared the test classroom and worksheets. It took about a month to complete this solution. After implementing these steps, the teacher noticed significant improvement in the teachers' skills and their ability to teach well. The teacher enjoyed the process despite the challenges and found the end result to be quite good.","Pdf":"https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3280/Improving_Teacher_Skills.pdf","Images":"","Transcript Link":"tgpq0ingljmpz4clpp2qpim7pgb011a7","state":"bihar","event_pushed_at":"2026-01-06T15:28:59.203957"}"""

  val EVENT_2: String = """{"id":"3,281","Title":"How a Group of Parents and Community Members Tackled the Challenge of Insufficient Books in Their School","User name":"","designation":"Shikshak","location":"Patna, Bihar","District":"Patna","organization":"Ramkrishna School","Report Created At":"July 3, 2025, 9:19 AM","objective":"To improve the education in Ramkrishna School by providing necessary books to the students","Challenges":"Children were not able to study well due to lack of books because there was no proper funding","Action Steps":"['Write a letter to the school management']","impact":"The problem was solved","duration":"10 years","blurb":"I, Rakesh, solved the problem of lack of books in my school by writing a letter to the school management. The kids and the position helped me write the letter. It took 10 years to complete this solution, but the problem was finally solved.","masked_blurb":"I solved the problem of lack of books in my school by writing a letter to the school management. The kids and the position helped me write the letter. It took 10 years to complete this solution, but the problem was finally solved.","content":"Rakesh, a shikshak at Ramkrishna School in Patna, Bihar, noticed that children were not able to study well due to a lack of books in the school. The main reason for this problem was the lack of proper funding. To solve this problem, Rakesh wrote a letter to the school management. The kids and the position worked together with Rakesh to help write the letter. It took 10 years to complete this solution. Rakesh did not face any challenges while performing these tasks. The outcome of this solution was that the problem was solved. Rakesh worked together with the kids and the position to achieve this outcome.","masked_content":"A shikshak at Ramkrishna School in Patna, Bihar, noticed that children were not able to study well due to a lack of books in the school. The main reason for this problem was the lack of proper funding. To solve this problem, the shikshak wrote a letter to the school management. The kids and the position worked together with the shikshak to help write the letter. It took 10 years to complete this solution. The shikshak did not face any challenges while performing these tasks. The outcome of this solution was that the problem was solved. The shikshak worked together with the kids and the position to achieve this outcome.","Pdf":"https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3281/Improving_Education_in_Ramkrishna_School.pdf","Images":"https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3281/1751514555-1000078256.png | https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3281/1751514563-1000078247.png","Transcript Link":"51g9y4unkmez4l3q645jhku8onzl201d","state":"bihar","event_pushed_at":"2026-01-06T15:28:59.227081"}"""

  val EVENT_3: String = """{"id":"3,283","Title":"How Community Members Addressed the Shortage of Benches in the Classroom","User name":"Prem","designation":"Manager","location":"Manchalwadi, Patna, Bihar","District":"Patna","organization":"Hegade Mahasangh","Report Created At":"July 3, 2025, 9:56 AM","objective":"To provide a comfortable learning environment for students by addressing the shortage of benches in the classroom","Challenges":"The school classroom lacked benches due to lack of funding with the school management","Action Steps":"['We wrote a letter to the school management regarding the shortage of benches', 'Poshak and Position worked with me to convince the school management about the shortage of benches and brought this to the notice of the management']","impact":"New benches arrived in the school, and there was space for the children to sit","duration":"8 months","blurb":"I addressed the issue of a lack of benches in my school by writing a letter to the school management and working with Poshak and Position to convince them of the need for new benches. After 8 months, new benches arrived, providing enough space for all the children to sit.","masked_blurb":"I addressed the issue of a lack of benches in my school by writing a letter to the school management and working with colleagues to convince them of the need for new benches. After 8 months, new benches arrived, providing enough space for all the children to sit.","content":"Prem, the manager of Hegade Mahasangh, identified a significant problem in his school - the classroom lacked benches. He noted that the reason for this issue was a lack of funding with the school management. To address this problem, Prem took the initiative to write a letter to the school management regarding the shortage of benches. He worked closely with Poshak and Position, who helped convince the school management about the need for new benches and brought this issue to their notice. After 8 months of effort, the school management finally ordered new benches. With the arrival of the new benches, the school now has enough space for all the children to sit, marking a significant improvement in the learning environment. Throughout this process, Prem did not face any major challenges and was pleased to see the positive impact of his actions on the school. The new benches have not only provided a comfortable seating arrangement for the students but have also contributed to a more conducive learning environment. Prem's experience demonstrates the importance of persistence and collaboration in addressing educational problems and creating positive change in the community.","masked_content":"The manager of Hegade Mahasangh identified a significant problem in the school - the classroom lacked benches. The manager noted that the reason for this issue was a lack of funding with the school management. To address this problem, the manager took the initiative to write a letter to the school management regarding the shortage of benches. The manager worked closely with colleagues, who helped convince the school management about the need for new benches and brought this issue to their notice. After 8 months of effort, the school management finally ordered new benches. With the arrival of the new benches, the school now has enough space for all the children to sit, marking a significant improvement in the learning environment. Throughout this process, the manager did not face any major challenges and was pleased to see the positive impact of the actions on the school. The new benches have not only provided a comfortable seating arrangement for the students but have also contributed to a more conducive learning environment. The manager's experience demonstrates the importance of persistence and collaboration in addressing educational problems and creating positive change in the community.","Pdf":"https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3283/New_Benches_for_School.pdf","Images":"https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3283/1751516919-1000075971.png | https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3283/1751516824-1000078252.png | https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3283/1751516851-1000077174.png | https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3283/1751516885-1000076260.png | https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3283/1751516829-1000078255.png | https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3283/1751516866-1000076929.png | https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3283/1751516836-1000078110.jpg | https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3283/1751516894-1000076122.png | https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3283/1751516875-1000076682.png | https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3283/1751516907-1000076104.png","Transcript Link":"r1uvpnxxbw9el5vw80boom6vw4rch1z3","state":"bihar","event_pushed_at":"2026-01-06T15:28:59.229495"}"""

  val EVENT_4: String = """{"id":"3,296","Title":"Community came together to tackle flood-related barriers that restricted access to schools","User name":"","designation":"Student","location":"Patna","District":"Patna","organization":"","Report Created At":"July 3, 2025, 11:58 PM","objective":"To solve the problem of not being able to go to school due to floods","Challenges":"Students could not reach school during monsoon season because flooding made roads impassable and there was no alternative transportation available","Action Steps":"['Together we dream and demand tomorrow from the government', 'All the people of the village came together', 'Everyone is with us, we went to the officer']","impact":"The people of the village came together to solve the problem","duration":"Half an hour","blurb":"I, Ramu, a student, worked with my community to address the issue of not being able to attend school due to floods. We came together and met with an officer to demand a solution. Although I didn't notice any immediate changes, I'm hopeful that our efforts will lead to positive outcomes in the future.","masked_blurb":"I, a student, worked with my community to address the issue of not being able to attend school due to floods. We came together and met with an officer to demand a solution. Although I didn't notice any immediate changes, I'm hopeful that our efforts will lead to positive outcomes in the future.","content":"Ramu, a student, found himself unable to attend school due to the devastating floods in his area. He expressed his concerns, saying, \"I can't go to my school because of the floods.\" The reason for this problem was clear: the flood had made it impossible for him to access his school. Ramu and his community decided to take action, coming together to demand a solution from the government. As Ramu put it, \"Together we dream and demand tomorrow from the government.\" They met with an officer, and although Ramu initially felt uncertain about how to proceed, saying \"I did not know how to do the work, Pappu Bhaiya please tell me,\" the community's collective efforts eventually led to a sense of unity and purpose. The people of the village came together, and as Ramu said, \"All the people of the village came together... Everyone is with us, we went to the officer.\" Although the process was challenging, Ramu and his community persevered, driven by their determination to find a solution. When asked about the timeline, Ramu mentioned that they met for about half an hour. As for the outcome, Ramu noted that he didn't notice any immediate changes, saying, \"You will not see the work when the bridge is completed... Oh, when the flower hasn't turned into a flower yet.\" Despite this, Ramu's experience has likely had a lasting impact on him, and he may have gained valuable insights into the importance of community action and perseverance in the face of adversity. Ramu's story serves as a testament to the power of collective action and the potential for positive change, even in the face of seemingly insurmountable challenges.","masked_content":"A student found himself unable to attend school due to the devastating floods in his area. He expressed his concerns, saying, \"I can't go to my school because of the floods.\" The reason for this problem was clear: the flood had made it impossible for him to access his school. The student and his community decided to take action, coming together to demand a solution from the government. As the student put it, \"Together we dream and demand tomorrow from the government.\" They met with an officer, and although the student initially felt uncertain about how to proceed, saying \"I did not know how to do the work, please tell me,\" the community's collective efforts eventually led to a sense of unity and purpose. The people of the village came together, and as the student said, \"All the people of the village came together... Everyone is with us, we went to the officer.\" Although the process was challenging, the student and his community persevered, driven by their determination to find a solution. When asked about the timeline, the student mentioned that they met for about half an hour. As for the outcome, the student noted that he didn't notice any immediate changes, saying, \"You will not see the work when the bridge is completed... Oh, when the flower hasn't turned into a flower yet.\" Despite this, the student's experience has likely had a lasting impact on him, and he may have gained valuable insights into the importance of community action and perseverance in the face of adversity. The student's story serves as a testament to the power of collective action and the potential for positive change, even in the face of seemingly insurmountable challenges.","Pdf":"https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3296/Ramu.pdf","Images":"","Transcript Link":"4oisz0xvjrz0fdil854jrhknf2xb3b2x","state":"bihar","event_pushed_at":"2026-01-06T15:28:59.231531"}"""

  val EVENT_5: String = """{"id":"3,845","Title":"How a College Student Overcame Societal Pressure to Pursue Education","User name":"","designation":"College student","location":"Munni, Bandra, Muzaffarpur, Bihar","District":"Muzaffarpur","organization":"","Report Created At":"July 30, 2025, 1:25 PM","objective":"To empower girls through education and gain support from their families and community.","Challenges":"Girls were dropping out of school due to early marriage because of societal pressure and lack of awareness about the importance of girls","Action Steps":"['The user participated in the teenage stage and gained self-confidence.', 'The user explained her wishes to her mother and friends.', 'The user brought her mother to the teenage stage and introduced her to her sister.']","impact":"The user’s mother now supports her education and wants her to study. The user has gained self-confidence and is able to explain her wishes to her mother and friends.","duration":"2-3 weeks","blurb":"I, Demo Bihari, was able to convince my mother to support my education after participating in the teenage stage and gaining self-confidence. With the help of Lucky didi, I was able to make a positive change in my life and am now supported by my mother to pursue my education. I noticed a significant change in my mother’s attitude, who now wants me to study and is supporting me a lot.","masked_blurb":"I was able to convince my mother to support my education after participating in the teenage stage and gaining self-confidence. With the help of a didi, I was able to make a positive change in my life and am now supported by my mother to pursue my education. I noticed a significant change in my mother’s attitude, who now wants me to study and is supporting me a lot.","content":"Demo Bihari, a college student, had noticed that girls in her community were being forced to get married at a young age, which was halting their education. She was afraid of society and her parents did not agree with her decision to pursue her education. However, after participating in the teenage stage and gaining self-confidence, she explained her wishes to her mother and friends. With the help of Lucky didi, who came to teach and explain the importance of education, Demo Bihari was able to convince her mother to support her education. Now, Demo Bihari and her mother attend the Kishori forum every month to discuss their wishes and aspirations. Initially, Demo Bihari faced challenges as her mother and friends did not agree with her, but she overcame them by introducing her mother to Lucky didi and explaining her wishes. It took 2-3 weeks for Demo Bihari and her mother to understand and come to an agreement. With Lucky didi’s guidance, Demo Bihari was able to make a positive change in her life and is now supported by her mother to pursue her education. Demo Bihari noticed a significant change in her mother’s attitude, who now wants her to study and is supporting her a lot.","masked_content":"A college student had noticed that girls in her community were being forced to get married at a young age, which was halting their education. She was afraid of society and her parents did not agree with her decision to pursue her education. However, after participating in the teenage stage and gaining self-confidence, she explained her wishes to her mother and friends. With the help of a didi who came to teach and explain the importance of education, the college student was able to convince her mother to support her education. Now, the college student and her mother attend the Kishori forum every month to discuss their wishes and aspirations. Initially, the college student faced challenges as her mother and friends did not agree with her, but she overcame them by introducing her mother to the didi and explaining her wishes. It took 2-3 weeks for the college student and her mother to understand and come to an agreement. With the didi’s guidance, the college student was able to make a positive change in her life and is now supported by her mother to pursue her education. The college student noticed a significant change in her mother’s attitude, who now wants her to study and is supporting her a lot.","Pdf":"https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3845/Empowering_Girls_Through_Education.pdf","Images":"","Transcript Link":"2o9q62mjvu5x9f4350wbb10d4ylfw8pf","state":"bihar","event_pushed_at":"2026-01-06T15:28:59.234229"}"""

  val EVENT_6: String = """{"id":"3,854","Title":"How Nidhi Kumari overcame the practice of child marriage to pursue her education","User name":"Nidhi Kumari","designation":"Vidyarthi","location":"Bandra Muzaffarpur Bihar","District":"Muzaffarpur","organization":"Kakhag Vidyalaya","Report Created At":"July 30, 2025, 4:10 PM","objective":"To increase the education of girls in the community by stopping child marriage","Challenges":"The practice of child marriage was preventing girls from continuing their education due to traditional beliefs and lack of awareness about the importance of girls","Action Steps":"['Nidhi and her mother participated in Shiksha Chaupal, where they came to know the importance of education and also came to know about the challenges like child marriage and understood the importance of education.', 'Nidhi took a resolution in her heart that she will study at least till 12th.', \"Nidhi and her mother together talked to Neeti's father and convinced him about this resolution.\", 'Jyoti Mahila Samakhya helped Nidhi take this pledge at Shiksha Chaupal and also helped her talk to the community']","impact":"The education of girls in the community was stopped early due to child marriage, but after Nidhi and her mother took a resolution to study at least till 12th, the courage of other girls and their mothers in the community also increased.","duration":"1 month","blurb":"I, Nidhi Kumari, stopped child marriage in my community by pursuing my education and convincing my family to support me. With the help of Jyoti Mahila Samakhya, I was able to take a pledge at Shiksha Chaupal and talk to my community about the importance of education. As a result, other girls and their mothers in the community also gained courage to pursue their education.","masked_blurb":"I stopped child marriage in my community by pursuing my education and convincing my family to support me. With the help of Jyoti Mahila Samakhya, I was able to take a pledge at Shiksha Chaupal and talk to my community about the importance of education. As a result, other girls and their mothers in the community also gained courage to pursue their education.","content":"Nidhi Kumari, a student at Kakhag Vidyalaya in Bandra, Muzaffarpur, Bihar, noticed that child marriage was a significant problem in her community, leading to girls dropping out of school early. She decided to take action and participated in Shiksha Chaupal with her mother, where they learned about the importance of education and the challenges posed by child marriage. Nidhi resolved to study at least till 12th grade and convinced her mother and father to support her decision. Despite facing opposition from the community, Nidhi persevered and achieved academic success, becoming an example for others to follow. With the help of Jyoti Mahila Samakhya, Nidhi was able to take her pledge to the community and encourage other girls and their mothers to pursue their education. As a result, the community began to see the value in education, and other girls gained the courage to continue their studies. Nidhi’s efforts took about a month to bear fruit, and she worked closely with the Jyoti Mahila Samakhya group to make it happen. Through her journey, Nidhi learned the importance of perseverance and community support in driving positive change. She hopes that her story will inspire others to take action against child marriage and promote education in their communities.","masked_content":"A student at Kakhag Vidyalaya in Bandra, Muzaffarpur, Bihar, noticed that child marriage was a significant problem in her community, leading to girls dropping out of school early. She decided to take action and participated in Shiksha Chaupal with her mother, where they learned about the importance of education and the challenges posed by child marriage. The student resolved to study at least till 12th grade and convinced her mother and father to support her decision. Despite facing opposition from the community, the student persevered and achieved academic success, becoming an example for others to follow. With the help of Jyoti Mahila Samakhya, the student was able to take her pledge to the community and encourage other girls and their mothers to pursue their education. As a result, the community began to see the value in education, and other girls gained the courage to continue their studies. The student’s efforts took about a month to bear fruit, and she worked closely with the Jyoti Mahila Samakhya group to make it happen. Through her journey, the student learned the importance of perseverance and community support in driving positive change. She hopes that her story will inspire others to take action against child marriage and promote education in their communities.","Pdf":"https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3854/Nidhi_Kumaris_Resolution_to_Study.pdf","Images":"","Transcript Link":"wgrtc6a56obamxaun6d7y5ytxit167pz","state":"bihar","event_pushed_at":"2026-01-06T15:28:59.241121"}"""

  val EVENT_7: String = """{"id":"3,880","Title":"How Community Members Came Together to Support Girls","User name":"Vandana Kumari","designation":"Student","location":"Hattha Village, Bandra Block, Muzaffarpur, Bihar","District":"Muzaffarpur","organization":"Utkramit Madhya Vidyalaya","Report Created At":"July 31, 2025, 8:41 PM","objective":"To improve girls education in the community","Challenges":"Girls were dropping out of school due to poverty and lack of awareness about the importance of education","Action Steps":"['Conducted education chaupal', 'Got Aadhar card made for teenage girls', 'Got caste and residential cards made']","impact":"There has been an improvement in the interest of girls towards studies","duration":"2 months","blurb":"I addressed the problem of girls being deprived of education in my community by organizing education chaupals and motivating girls to attend meetings. I also helped them obtain necessary documents like Aadhar cards and caste certificates. As a result, there has been an improvement in the interest of girls towards studies.","masked_blurb":"I addressed the problem of girls being deprived of education in my community by organizing education chaupals and motivating girls to attend meetings. I also helped them obtain necessary documents like Aadhar cards and caste certificates. As a result, there has been an improvement in the interest of girls towards studies.","content":"Vandana Kumari, a student from Utkramit Madhya Vidyalaya Hatyaa, noticed that girls in her community were being deprived of education. Many girls were dropping out of school after the fourth, third, or fifth grade due to poverty and a lack of understanding about the importance of education. Vandana decided to take action and organized an education chaupal, where she took an oath with the community members to address this issue. She helped 12 teenage girls obtain Aadhar cards and 21 girls receive caste and residential certificates. Vandana also motivated girls to attend meetings and take a pledge to support each other in their studies. Despite facing opposition from the community, Vandana continued to explain the importance of education to the parents of the teenage girls. With the support of Jyoti Mahila Samakhya's sister Ragini, who helped them at the RTPS counter at the block level, Vandana was able to make a positive impact. Over a period of two months, Vandana noticed an improvement in the interest of girls towards studies. Additionally, boys who were not attending school earlier and were instead doing household chores or playing, are now ready to go to school. Those who are interested in studying are also attending school. Vandana's efforts have made a significant difference in her community, and she continues to work towards promoting education and empowering girls.","masked_content":"A student from Utkramit Madhya Vidyalaya Hatyaa noticed that girls in the community were being deprived of education. Many girls were dropping out of school after the fourth, third, or fifth grade due to poverty and a lack of understanding about the importance of education. The student decided to take action and organized an education chaupal, where the student took an oath with the community members to address this issue. The student helped 12 teenage girls obtain Aadhar cards and 21 girls receive caste and residential certificates. The student also motivated girls to attend meetings and take a pledge to support each other in their studies. Despite facing opposition from the community, the student continued to explain the importance of education to the parents of the teenage girls. With the support of Jyoti Mahila Samakhya's sister, who helped them at the RTPS counter at the block level, the student was able to make a positive impact. Over a period of two months, the student noticed an improvement in the interest of girls towards studies. Additionally, boys who were not attending school earlier and were instead doing household chores or playing, are now ready to go to school. Those who are interested in studying are also attending school. The student's efforts have made a significant difference in the community, and the student continues to work towards promoting education and empowering girls.","Pdf":"https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3880/Improving_Girls.pdf","Images":"","Transcript Link":"mq52f8zwvpakk2i8xirzcycxy1go56bp","state":"bihar","event_pushed_at":"2026-01-06T15:28:59.251963"}"""

  val EVENT_8: String = """{"id":"3,881","Title":"How Community Members Tackled the Practice of Child Marriage to Promote Girls","User name":"Sabreen Khaatoon","designation":"","location":"Rampur Dayal Bandra Muzaffarpur","District":"Muzaffarpur","organization":"Meena Manch","Report Created At":"July 31, 2025, 8:47 PM","objective":"To empower girls through education and raise awareness about their rights","Challenges":"Girls were unable to continue their education due to lack of awareness about their rights and the importance of education","Action Steps":"['Provided information about education and its importance', 'Explained the importance of education and rights to girls', 'Encouraged girls to speak up and raise their voices against problems and evil practices']","impact":"Awareness towards education increased among girls and women","duration":"1 month","blurb":"I, Sabreen Khaatoon, addressed the issue of girls' lack of knowledge about their rights, which led to their deprivation of education. Through Meena Manch, I provided information about education and rights, and as a result, many girls joined school and started speaking up for themselves. I faced challenges, but my leadership role gave me the strength to move ahead.","masked_blurb":"I addressed the issue of girls’ lack of knowledge about their rights, which led to their deprivation of education. Through Meena Manch, I provided information about education and rights, and as a result, many girls joined school and started speaking up for themselves. I faced challenges, but a leadership role gave me the strength to move ahead.","content":"Sabreen Khaatoon, a resident of Rampur Dayal Bandra Muzaffarpur, noticed that girls in her village were unable to speak up for themselves due to a lack of knowledge about their rights, leading to deprivation of education. She decided to take action through Meena Manch, a program that provides information about education and rights. The girls were explained the importance of education and their rights, and as a result, many girls who were previously unable to attend school began to join. The girls who were once unable to speak up started speaking fearlessly and raising their voices against problems and evil practices happening to women and teenagers. Despite facing challenges such as taunts from other girls and negative comments from the community, Sabreen found the strength to move ahead through her role in leadership. With the help of Soni Kumari, the catalyst of Meena Manch, Sabreen was able to complete this task in one month. The outcome was a significant increase in awareness towards education among girls and women.","masked_content":"A resident of Rampur Dayal Bandra Muzaffarpur noticed that girls in the village were unable to speak up for themselves due to a lack of knowledge about their rights, leading to deprivation of education. The resident decided to take action through Meena Manch, a program that provides information about education and rights. The girls were explained the importance of education and their rights, and as a result, many girls who were previously unable to attend school began to join. The girls who were once unable to speak up started speaking fearlessly and raising their voices against problems and evil practices happening to women and teenagers. Despite facing challenges such as taunts from other girls and negative comments from the community, the resident found the strength to move ahead through a role in leadership. With the help of the catalyst of Meena Manch, the resident was able to complete this task in one month. The outcome was a significant increase in awareness towards education among girls and women.","Pdf":"https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3881/Empowering_Girls_through_Education.pdf","Images":"","Transcript Link":"7xnoci5iu7s6zvpd0iyrox2trm605k2k","state":"bihar","event_pushed_at":"2026-01-06T15:28:59.270234"}"""

  val EVENT_9: String = """{"id":"3,883","Title":"Community Members Came Together to Support Education for Female Adolescents Through Music and Games","User name":"Vasundhara Devi","designation":"Sahayika","location":"Muzaffarpur, Bihar","District":"Muzaffarpur","organization":"Anganbadi","Report Created At":"July 31, 2025, 8:55 PM","objective":"To improve education in Muzaffarpur by addressing the issue of poverty and lack of attention to studies","Challenges":"Female adolescents were dropping out of school due to lack of interest and support, because of societal pressures and limited access to engaging educational activities","Action Steps":"['The community helped take children to school from their homes', 'Held a meeting of the task force', \"Held a meeting of the women's group\"]","impact":"Female adolescents were educated in the field of music through songs and games","duration":"15 days","blurb":"I addressed the issue of ablution of information in my community by taking children to school and educating female adolescents through music and games. With the help of my team, we were able to make a positive impact in just 15 days.","masked_blurb":"I addressed the issue of ablution of information in my community by taking children to school and educating female adolescents through music and games. With the help of my team, we were able to make a positive impact in just 15 days.","content":"Vasundhara Devi, a dedicated sahayika, has been working tirelessly to improve education in her community in Muzaffarpur, Bihar. She noticed that the main problem was the ablution of information, which was affecting the children's ability to focus on their studies. The reasons for this problem were that people in the community were more focused on their daily work and didn't pay attention to the importance of education. \n\nTo address this issue, Vasundhara Devi took a multi-step approach. Firstly, she ensured that the community was involved in taking the children to school from their homes. This not only encouraged the children to attend school regularly but also helped to build a sense of responsibility among the community members. \n\nAdditionally, Vasundhara Devi organized meetings with the task force and women's groups to discuss the importance of education and the need to support the children in their academic pursuits. She also used creative methods such as music and games to educate female adolescents, making learning a fun and engaging experience for them. \n\nOne of the significant challenges Vasundhara Devi faced was discussing the issue of dropouts and nominations based on education. However, with the support of her team, she was able to overcome this challenge and make a positive impact in just 15 days. \n\nThe outcome of Vasundhara Devi's efforts was remarkable. She noticed significant changes in the community, with more children attending school regularly and showing a keen interest in their studies. The community members also became more supportive and encouraging, recognizing the importance of education in improving their children's lives. \n\nVasundhara Devi's experience is a testament to the power of community involvement and creative approaches to education. Her dedication and hard work have made a lasting impact on the lives of the children and community members in Muzaffarpur, Bihar. \n\nIn conclusion, Vasundhara Devi's story highlights the importance of addressing the root causes of educational problems and working collaboratively with the community to find solutions. Her approach has not only improved the educational outcomes of the children but has also empowered the community members to take ownership of their children's education. \n\nAs Vasundhara Devi continues to work towards improving education in her community, her story serves as an inspiration to others who are passionate about making a positive difference in the lives of children and community members. With her unwavering dedication and commitment to education, Vasundhara Devi is sure to achieve even greater success in the future.","masked_content":"A dedicated sahayika has been working tirelessly to improve education in her community in Muzaffarpur, Bihar. She noticed that the main problem was the ablution of information, which was affecting the children's ability to focus on their studies. The reasons for this problem were that people in the community were more focused on their daily work and didn't pay attention to the importance of education. To address this issue, the sahayika took a multi-step approach. Firstly, she ensured that the community was involved in taking the children to school from their homes. This not only encouraged the children to attend school regularly but also helped to build a sense of responsibility among the community members. Additionally, the sahayika organized meetings with the task force and women's groups to discuss the importance of education and the need to support the children in their academic pursuits. She also used creative methods such as music and games to educate female adolescents, making learning a fun and engaging experience for them. One of the significant challenges the sahayika faced was discussing the issue of dropouts and nominations based on education. However, with the support of her team, she was able to overcome this challenge and make a positive impact in just 15 days. The outcome of the sahayika's efforts was remarkable. She noticed significant changes in the community, with more children attending school regularly and showing a keen interest in their studies. The community members also became more supportive and encouraging, recognizing the importance of education in improving their children's lives. The sahayika's experience is a testament to the power of community involvement and creative approaches to education. Her dedication and hard work have made a lasting impact on the lives of the children and community members in Muzaffarpur, Bihar. In conclusion, the sahayika's story highlights the importance of addressing the root causes of educational problems and working collaboratively with the community to find solutions. Her approach has not only improved the educational outcomes of the children but has also empowered the community members to take ownership of their children's education. As the sahayika continues to work towards improving education in her community, her story serves as an inspiration to others who are passionate about making a positive difference in the lives of children and community members. With her unwavering dedication and commitment to education, the sahayika is sure to achieve even greater success in the future.","Pdf":"https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3883/Empowering_Education_in_Muzaffarpur.pdf","Images":"","Transcript Link":"0d3a3kau7d0e9n44qi7pjxouqxi9f6er","state":"bihar","event_pushed_at":"2026-01-06T15:28:59.272595"}"""

  val EVENT_10: String = """{"id":"3,884","Title":"How a group of parents came together to tackle financial barriers that restricted girls","User name":"Savita","designation":"Task Force Group Adhyaksh","location":"Dhanahra Village No. 11 under Shivhar Dumri Katsari","District":"Sheohar","organization":"Srishti Mahila Samakhya Shivhar","Report Created At":"August 1, 2025, 9:27 AM","objective":"To educate girls and increase awareness about the importance of education","Challenges":"Girls were dropping out of school due to lack of money because their parents prioritized immediate financial needs over long-term educational benefits","Action Steps":"['Savita requested her mother to let her study', 'Savita requested her father to let her study in a good school', 'CC and BC talked to their parents and discussed about admission']","impact":"The desire of the people to educate girls increased","duration":"15 to 20 days","blurb":"I, Savita, was able to get admitted in class 11 with the help of CC and BC, who talked to their parents and discussed about admission. I faced challenges, but I was able to overcome them and achieve my goal. The desire of the people of Yes to educate girls increased, and I was able to make a positive change in my community.","masked_blurb":"I was able to get admitted in class 11 with the help of CC and BC, who talked to their parents and discussed about admission. I faced challenges, but I was able to overcome them and achieve my goal. The desire of the people of Yes to educate girls increased, and I was able to make a positive change in my community.","content":"Savita, a student from Dhanahra Village No. 11 under Shivhar Dumri Katsari, was determined to pursue her education. She was doing her 10th exam and wanted to study in 11th, but her father was refusing due to lack of money. Savita requested her mother to let her study and her father to let her study in a good school because she had taken an oath in six chaupals and in some other kishori manch that girls should study in 12th. She faced challenges as her parents used to refuse saying that now there is no money, where will you study, what will you do. However, with the help of CC and BC, who talked to their parents and discussed about admission, Savita was able to get admitted in class 11. The desire of the people of Yes to educate girls increased, and Savita was able to achieve her goal. She worked on this task for 15 to 20 days and was able to overcome the challenges she faced. Savita’s experience shows that with determination and hard work, anything is possible. She was able to make a positive change in her community and inspire others to do the same. Savita’s story is an inspiration to all the girls who want to pursue their education and make a difference in their communities. She proved that with the right support and mindset, girls can achieve anything they set their minds to. Savita’s journey is a testament to the power of education and the impact it can have on individuals and communities. She was able to break down barriers and challenge societal norms, and her story will continue to inspire and motivate others to do the same. In the end, Savita was able to achieve her goal and make a positive change in her community, and her story will be remembered as an inspiration to all.","masked_content":"A student from Dhanahra Village No. 11 under Shivhar Dumri Katsari, was determined to pursue her education. She was doing her 10th exam and wanted to study in 11th, but her father was refusing due to lack of money. She requested her mother to let her study and her father to let her study in a good school because she had taken an oath in six chaupals and in some other kishori manch that girls should study in 12th. She faced challenges as her parents used to refuse saying that now there is no money, where will you study, what will you do. However, with the help of CC and BC, who talked to their parents and discussed about admission, she was able to get admitted in class 11. The desire of the people of Yes to educate girls increased, and she was able to achieve her goal. She worked on this task for 15 to 20 days and was able to overcome the challenges she faced. Her experience shows that with determination and hard work, anything is possible. She was able to make a positive change in her community and inspire others to do the same. Her story is an inspiration to all the girls who want to pursue their education and make a difference in their communities. She proved that with the right support and mindset, girls can achieve anything they set their minds to. Her journey is a testament to the power of education and the impact it can have on individuals and communities. She was able to break down barriers and challenge societal norms, and her story will continue to inspire and motivate others to do the same. In the end, she was able to achieve her goal and make a positive change in her community, and her story will be remembered as an inspiration to all.","Pdf":"https://mohini-static.shikshalokam.org/chatbot/storymedia/3884/Savitas_Journey_to_Education.pdf","Images":"","Transcript Link":"xa8ftum46132o41a278uouo9ojzqcwj9","state":"bihar","event_pushed_at":"2026-01-06T15:28:59.275105"}"""
}